{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 20, :comments ["<b>Wide is Gad.</b> He blessed him thus because He gave him a broad land, a land of livestock." "<b>And he tore arm also skull.</b> Since it says <b>also skull</b>, it implies that he strikes the arm first. How so? When Gad comes to raise his hand to strike his opponent, the opponent raises his hand against the sword, and so Gad cuts off the arm first and strikes the head and kills him with a single blow."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 33, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:55:28.814305738Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}